<blockquote>
<p>The entity will consume approximately 30 humans over a two day period once per month and will expand its feeding area should humans be scarce</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>D-Class fed to SCP-XXXX</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Should there be a shortage of D-Class during feeding episodes then civilians are permitted to be used at the discretion of two members of Level 3 personnel</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hasn't the Foundation tried to kill this? I mean, 30 people once a month for a year - that's 360 people sacrificed to the dark underlord every twelve months. Wouldn't this warrant the research of additional containment options, if not termination? The report doesn't really specify how implacable the thing is. Even 682, the immortal reptile who literally can adapt to any threat, is contained relatively easily in a vat of acid. Although, 682 tends to be a bad example.</p>
<p>Still, I think the point is made.</p>

