					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kholettedrake" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1909832); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1909832&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467139" alt="KholetteDrake" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1909832)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kholettedrake" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1909832); return false;" >KholetteDrake</a></span> <span class="odate time_1437804944 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Jul 2015 06:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2345215">
									

<p>The Foundation hasn't tried to kill it because Secure, Contain, Protect. Not Slaughter, Cut, Perforate. That said&#8230;</p>
<p>I downvoted for two reasons: one, redactions and blackboxing in the containment. How is someone supposed to know where to contain it if that information has been hidden? Two, it breaks suspension of disbelief in that this creature feeds exclusively on humans. People haven't been around that long. Even less time have people been in places where this creature would feed. It would be a truly breathtaking series of circumstances that caused evolution to select for a humans-only diet when it lives in areas that A) have hot springs and B) have humans near those hot springs. Then there is the numbers thing. In order for it to get enough energy from humans to drive its 300 meters of body, it would need thousands, possibly hundreds of thousands of us each day.</p>
<p>Although, I do like the implication that the people it eats are living it up in a sunny paradise inside it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
