				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/superjotunn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2161351); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2161351&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467139" alt="SuperJotunn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2161351)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/superjotunn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2161351); return false;" >SuperJotunn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1437806045 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Jul 2015 06:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2345222">
									

<p>To be honest I kind of personally don't buy the idea that the Foundation wouldn't try and kill a thing if they had very good reason to think that would help with the &quot;Protect&quot; part in a big way. I think that they're pack rats and they do want to secure and contain anomalous things, but sometimes termination is the best option. Not always but sometimes. That's neither here nor there just a thing I think.</p>
<p>I can undo the blackboxes and give a name for what hotels are actually there, that's a fair enough criticism. The redaction I don't think is an important thing though. You still know how it's being contained. If they're going to actually have to deal with it then they'll have the clearance to know exactly where it is. That's just my thoughts, I can change it if a lot of people think i'm wrong in that.</p>
<p>I know this isn't present in the article but my idea is that the creature hasn't always been on earth/in this dimension, it popped up because there's intelligent life on this little chunk of rock to render certain services to them. And I feel like I can be handwave-y about extradimensional creatures' daily intake needs, especially because it's not actually eating any of the people that are going down the tube.</p>
<p>I'm glad you like the end and you have fair enough reasons for downvoting, those are just my thoughts in reply.</p>

