<p>Pros:</p>
<ul>
<li>This SCP really harkens back to the older stylistics and SCP-2086, which go all out to describe a creature's habits and all that. Nostalgic value, I suppose.</li>
</ul>
<p>Cons:</p>
<ul>
<li>The horror moment that one can be fed to a monster is not that well-done. Why must humans be sacrificed? Can the Foundation not force it to adapt to the taste of a cow?</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">* I do agree with Whatopercy2 on the excessive loss of lives to maintain just one thing, that may not be that all important. It's quite a fallacy since one writes SCPs under the assumption that one has all the resources needed, but a real organisation like the Foundation would be eternally strapped for resources.</span> EDIT: In light of edit, switch to neutrality.</p>
<p>Verdict: Neutral vote</p>

