<p>Neutral vote, since the concept is kind of silly to me personally, but I can also respect the existence of a subterranean bug that sucks people into its party zone on the mainlist.</p>
<p>I did find the fact that the Foundation leaps from &quot;non-standard genetic structure&quot; to &quot;extradimensional&quot; to be kind of silly. That's a completely absurd conclusion, as well as an abuse of the phrase &quot;extradimensional&quot; to mean &quot;from some place what we don't know about&quot; (albeit an abuse committed daily by just about everyone here). I also don't care for censored dates that only involve one digit of the year. Why would it be okay to know which decade something occurred in, but not the specific year? I'd consider fixing those.</p>

