			<div class="content" id="post-content-2348025">
									

<p>I spent a while thinking about the extradimensional bit so i'll see if I can explain the logic and maybe come up with an idea of how to fix the leap the Foundation makes.<br />
So for starters, the creature is extradimensional. It does come from a place very much unlike our own which is not in our universe and it didn't get here by travelling spatially. But hey, I don't have in-universe ways to show that so it's a fair enough criticism to say that the Foundation makes an unjustified leap. However I do make the specification that the non-standard genetic structure &quot;possibly suggests&quot; the extradimensional bit, rather than stating it as something they have reached a consensus about.<br />
Again, my expression of this could very well have way missed the mark but by non-standard genetic structure I meant something that doesn't even resemble a genetic structure in the sense that we understand it.<br />
You can be the judge of whether I just expressed the underlying thinking poorly or whether the thinking still seems flawed.</p>
<p>Fair enough call about the blackboxes, will definitely get to that after the contest is over.</p>

